From a947d3de9302222ea093e6989049e765f465d182 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 23:28:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix analytics gaps, nav CTA clipping, and popup timing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Four issues found while auditing GA4 and Search Console.

Analytics blind spots
about.html, speaking.html, testimonials.html and quiz.html had no GA
tag at all. about.html is the site's top organic landing page — 16 of
40 search clicks over the last three months — so roughly 40% of organic
search traffic was invisible in Analytics. Added the standard
G-2QBSJ9PRRQ snippet to all four.

Duplicate homepage in reporting
The nav logo linked to index.html on every page, so GA counted "/" and
"/index.html" as two separate pages and split homepage metrics between
them. All internal home links now point at "/".

Header CTA clipped between ~960px and ~1050px
The desktop nav needed ~1036px but the container gave it less, so the
"Free Session, No Pitch" button overflowed and rendered as a blank
black rectangle — the only persistently visible CTA on the site.
Added flex-wrap to the nav so it wraps instead of overflowing, plus a
1400px breakpoint that tightens padding, gaps and icon sizes to keep
one row down to ~1250px. Verified clean from 390px to 1600px.

Popup covering the primary CTA
The homepage newsletter modal fired on a 13-second timer, which landed
squarely on "Book a free coaching session" for anyone reading the hero
at normal speed. The modal now never opens while a booking CTA is on
screen; a trigger that lands in that window is deferred and retried
rather than cancelled, so capture still happens once the CTA scrolls
away. Timer moved from 13s to 45s; the 55% scroll trigger is unchanged.

Booking page
Every CTA pointed at free-session.html, which is a five-field intake
form — the Calendly link was hidden inside the success card and only
appeared after submitting. Added a visible "Pick a time on my calendar"
option in the hero and beside the form, tracked as booking_direct_click
so the two paths can be compared. Also fixed the form aside, which
promised times by email within two business days while the success card
and confirmation page both describe self-service booking.

