From 948da7676f9950144d80c13603313354a02bb3ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 23:39:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Put proof before price, and specialty paths after the
 offer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two ordering changes that follow from the funnel data: 18 people reached
a coaching page last month and none clicked through to book.

coaching.html
"Why it works" — the MD / medical-educator / made-the-pivot-herself
credential block — now sits above the pricing instead of two screens
below it. Readers were meeting $1,200-$4,000 before any reason to
believe the person behind it.

"Specialty paths" — the three cards linking out to physician, ikigai and
career-reinvention pages — moves from immediately before the pricing to
immediately after it. It was routing people off the page at the exact
point the page was meant to close, and each destination is another long
page with its own funnel.

New order: hero, why not a platform, why it works, pricing, specialty
paths, how it works, is this for you, FAQ, location, book.

index.html
The client testimonial moves from screen 8 to directly above "Pick the
door that fits", so the first mention of price is preceded by someone
vouching for the work.

Verified: identical document height on both pages (no content lost),
no JS errors, nav clean from 390px to 1600px, and the homepage popup
still defers while a booking CTA is on screen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
